message: "If you use CZ-DSL, the toolchain, or the New York Harbor benchmark case, please cite both the paper and the software release."
title: "CZ-DSL: A Plug-in Atomic Domain-Specific Language with Geometric-Algebra Reversibility for Coastal-Zone Geographic Information Modeling"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Yu
    given-names: Zhaoyuan
    affiliation: "Nanjing Normal University, Nanjing, China"
    email: yuzhaoyuan@njnu.edu.cn
    orcid: ""   # TODO: add the ORCID iD before release
repository-code: "https://github.com/mapleyustat/CZ-DSL"
url: "https://github.com/mapleyustat/CZ-DSL"
abstract: >-
  CZ-DSL is a domain-specific language for coastal-zone complex systems. It
  organises 43 atomic components into seven plug-in groups and a four-level
  hierarchical classification, and integrates heterogeneous coastal data with its
  spatio-temporal datum, geometry, feature attributes, spatio-temporal processes
  and governing mechanisms into a single structured scenario that supports
  retrieval, query, computation and cross-application switching. The repository
  contains the language specification, the XSD and JSON Schema, a Python
  toolchain (scene builder, validator, compiler), a Rust frontend under
  development, and a fully reproducible real-data benchmark case for New York
  Harbor.
